  "_README": [
    "Static reference table: NFL stadium name (as it appears verbatim in",
    "data/raw/*/schedules.parquet's `stadium` column) -> (lat, lon, IANA tz,",
    "city). Built 2026-08-19 for ENV-03/ENV-04 (scripts/",
    "nfl_travel_rest_battery_screen.py). No stadium lat/lon table existed in",
    "this repo before (verified absent by grep 2026-08-19).",
    "",
    "Coordinates are reported general knowledge (not fetched from a live API",
    "this session), sanity-checked via computed great-circle distance against",
    "well-known city-pair mileages before use -- see docs/travel_rest_battery.md",
    "'Coordinate sanity check' section for the measured check.",
    "",
    "Keyed by exact `stadium` string (not `stadium_id`): stadium_id is NOT a",
    "reliable physical-location key for neutral-site/international games --",
    "nflverse leaves stadium_id set to the schedule-designated HOME team's own",
    "code (e.g. DAL00) even when `stadium` correctly names the true venue",
    "(e.g. 'Maracana Stadium'). Renamed stadiums at the same physical site",
    "(e.g. Denver's three names) get separate entries with identical/near-",
    "identical coordinates -- simple and correct, slightly redundant.",
    "",
    "tz is an IANA zone name; game-date-specific UTC offset (DST-aware) is",
    "computed at scoring time via Python's stdlib zoneinfo, not hardcoded here.",
    "",
    "Covers every `stadium` name appearing in REG games 2009-2025 (the scored",
    "window) plus a few 2026 (future, unscored) international venues for",
    "documentation completeness -- see docs/travel_rest_battery.md for the",
    "unresolved-name list (none within 2009-2025)."
